# Feature: runtime output via libSystem `write`.
# expect: stdout "hello world\n"
# expect: exit 0
# `print` takes a `str` ({ptr,len}); string literals live in __cstring and are
# addressed PIE-safely with adrp/add. `write` is bound from libSystem via a
# chained-fixup into __got. (exit is still dyld's, on main's return.)
fn main() {
    print("hello world\n")
}
